  "overview": {
    "query": "best changelog tool for saas",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The best changelog and release notes tools for SaaS depend on your team size, whether you need an all-in-one product loop (feedback and roadmaps), or just automated developer updates .",
        "refs": [0]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Top Changelog Tools for SaaS"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Frill: Best for startups wanting an all-in-one suite. It combines a changelog/announcements widget with a feedback board, public roadmap, and surveys starting at $25/month .",
            "refs": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "FeatureOS: Best for teams looking for deep custom domains, scheduling, multi-language support, and tight integration with feedback boards and roadmaps.",
            "refs": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "Canny: Best for product-led teams already using it for feature voting and user feedback, though the free/lower tiers have strict user caps.",
            "refs": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "Beamer: Best for in-app notifications and newsfeeds that pop up right inside your web application to drive high visibility.",
            "refs": [0]
          },
          {
            "text": "LaunchNotes: Best for enterprise SaaS companies needing advanced audience segmentation, stakeholder updates, and strict access controls.",
            "refs": [0]
          },
          {
            "text": "ReleaseNotes.io / Updatify: Best for developer-heavy workflows that want to auto-generate or convert git commits and pull requests directly into human-readable release notes.",
            "refs": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Key Features to Look For"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "In-App Widgets: Standalone pages are often ignored; look for a tool that lets you embed a notification bell or widget right inside your dashboard.",
            "refs": [0, 1]
          },
          {
            "text": "Feedback & Roadmap Loop: The top modern tools don't just broadcast updates—they connect the release back to the original customer feature request.",
            "refs": [0, 1]
